A51 USB: PIPE3 override in the PHY bring-up; USB works.

Boot 38's sweep found the missing piece at step 2: with the link told that
the (never initialised) USB3 PIPE PHY is idle, as the A51 kernel's
phy_exynos_usb_v3p1_pipe_ovrd does (LINK_CTRL PIPE3_FORCE_EN and
FORCE_RX_ELEC_IDLE, PHY_STATUS low; COMBO_PMA_CTRL LOW_PWRN), plus HSP
COMMONONN|EN_UTMISUSPEND for the DT's common_block_disable, the DWC3
applied the D+ pull-up and the host enumerated the CDC Ethernet gadget
within 2 s. Do this in a51_usb_phy_enable() and drop the sweep.

